fuzz_harness
*.o
crash-*
timeout-*
oom-*
leak-*

# Corpus growth discovered during local fuzzing is deliberately not
# committed - see "Should the corpus be committed?" in fuzz/README.md.
# libFuzzer names newly-discovered entries by content hash; this
# allowlists only the known seed files generate_corpus.py produces, so a
# stray `git add -A` after a local fuzzing session can't accidentally
# check in a pile of hash-named growth. Add a new seed here (and to
# generate_corpus.py) if you deliberately add one.
corpus/*
!corpus/malformed_length
!corpus/open_write_close
!corpus/opendir_readdir_close
!corpus/realpath
!corpus/rename_remove
!corpus/setstat_mkdir_rmdir
!corpus/stat_lstat_fstat
!corpus/symlink_readlink
